# Parallelism soundness Phase 3 (rule D1): passing a place rooted in a
# module-level global to an inout parameter is a write iff the callee may write
# through that parameter (the same mutation-mask decision as D3 for atomic
# objects), and a write to a global another thread reads is a data race.
# `describe` reads only and is accepted; `bump_by_ten` stores.
stdout_keep_match=Cannot pass an inout argument rooted in module-level global 'g'
